Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

---

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10.0  
**Scope:** 8 test methods in 1 class, marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`  
**Integration calibration applied:** Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test severities are adjusted per integration-test norms.

---

## Summary Dashboard

```
┌──────────┬─────────────┬────────────────┐
│ Severity │ Smell Count │ Affected Tests │
├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┤
│ High     │ 2           │ 2              │
│ Medium   │ 2           │ 2              │
│ Low      │ 0           │ 0              │
│ Total    │ 4           │ 4              │
└──────────┴─────────────┴────────────────┘
```

---

## Findings by Severity

### 1 · Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**Smell taxonomy:** Conditional Test Logic (testsmells.org #1)  
**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 96)  
**Risk:** The `if/else` on the loaded type means one branch is never exercised per run. If the repository always returns a base `User`, the `PremiumUser` path is dead code giving false coverage confidence.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — different assertions per branch
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests, each arranging the exact precondition it asserts:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### 2 · Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**Smell taxonomy:** Unknown Test / Empty Test (testsmells.org #4)  
**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)  
**Risk:** This test passes even if every insert silently corrupts data or is a no-op. The framework marks it green as long as no exception is thrown.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertions at all
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    const int batchSize = 100;
    for (int i = 0; i < batchSize; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(batchSize, users.Count);
}
```

---

### 3 · Sleepy Test — **Medium** *(downgraded from High — integration calibration)*

**Smell taxonomy:** Sleepy Test (testsmells.org #3)  
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)  
**Risk:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` adds 3 seconds of wall-clock time per run and is non-deterministic — a slower CI box may still fail. Additionally, `Thread.Sleep` is synchronous blocking inside an `async Task` method, wasting a thread-pool thread.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — hard-coded 3-second blocking sleep
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Use a polling loop with a timeout, or expose a `Task`-based notification signal:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with back-off instead of a blind sleep
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the timeout window.");
}
```

---

### 4 · Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**Smell taxonomy:** Assertion Roulette (testsmells.org, extended catalog)  
**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)  
**Risk:** 4 assertions with no failure messages. A red build gives only `Assert.AreEqual failed` — the developer must open the source to figure out which property mismatched.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 bare assertions, no messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add a message parameter to each assertion:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

---

## Smells Not Detected (15 of 19 — Clean)

| Smell | Status |
|---|---|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean — in-memory SQLite is hermetic, no external files/network/env |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean — no test exceeds 3 distinct production method calls; integration calibration also applies |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean — `3` and `10` in count assertions directly match the number of items just inserted |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean — no `ToString()`-based comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean — no `try`/`catch` in any test |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean — `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean — no `[Ignore]` or skipped tests |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean — each test exercises a distinct behavior |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean — uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean — class is meaningfully named |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean — no `Console.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean — no tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean — SQLite connection created fresh per test |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean |

---

## Smell-Free Tests Worth Highlighting

`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are all well-structured: clear arrange/act/assert, meaningful names, appropriate assertion count, and no unnecessary control flow.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1** | Assertion-Free Test (`BulkInsert`) | ~2 min | Highest risk — test is currently useless; one-line assertion fix |
| **2** | Conditional Test Logic (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | ~10 min | Hidden dead branch; split into two tests |
| **3** | Sleepy Test (`NotifyOnInsert`) | ~10 min | 3 s of CI time + flakiness risk; replace with poll loop |
| **4** | Assertion Roulette (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`) | ~2 min | Low effort, improves failure diagnostics |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests are clean. The two high-severity findings (#1 and #2) should be fixed immediately — they represent a false-pass risk and an untestable branch. The suite is otherwise well-designed for integration tests: hermetic fixture, proper lifecycle, no over-broad setup, and no unnecessary skips.
